      "text": "Eutrophication is the enrichment of a water body with nutrients (primarily phosphorus in freshwater), leading to increased primary production, algal blooms, oxygen depletion, and ecosystem degradation. It is the most widespread water quality problem globally and affects 30–40% of large lakes worldwide."
